[[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/3025840\">7045A10</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025841\">7045A24</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025847\">7045A43</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025848\">7045A44</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025857\">7045A86</a></p><p>1. Remove the heat pad by detaching it from the padding.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2005411.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the heater pad is\nnot damaged.</p><p>1. Position the heat pad (1a) and attach its adhesive side to the\npadding.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>The join strips (1b) must follow\nthe profile of the padding furrows, in order not to be under tension\nwhen the seat is used.</p></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2005412.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<p><a href=\"#/3025857\">7045A86</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025848\">7045A44</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025847\">7045A43</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025841\">7045A24</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025840\">7045A10</a></p>"]]